				<r3d:description language="eng">The World Ocean Database (WOD) is a collection of scientifically quality-controlled ocean  profile  and  plankton  data  that  includes  measurements  of  temperature,  salinity,  oxygen,  phosphate,  nitrate,  silicate,  chlorophyll,  alkalinity,  pH,  pCO2,  TCO2,  Tritium, Δ13Carbon, Δ14Carbon, Δ18Oxygen, Freon, Helium, Δ3Helium, Neon, and plankton.
WOD contains all data of &quot;World Data Service Oceanography&quot; (WDS-Oceanography).</r3d:description>
